# Frontend Engineering Standards

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Angular 18+ standalone (no NgModules), TypeScript `strict: true` + `strictTemplates`
- **UI**: Angular Material + CDK (M2/M3, theme tokens `--mat-sys-*`)
- **State**: NgRx Component Store (server) · Signals `signal/computed/effect` (local) · NgRx Store (global)
- **Async**: RxJS → convert to signals via `toSignal()`; unsubscribe with `takeUntilDestroyed()` or `async` pipe
- **Forms**: Reactive Forms with typed `FormGroup<T>`; **HTTP**: `HttpClient` + functional interceptors

---

## Architecture

### Container / Presentational
- **Container** (`features/<feature>/pages/`): injects services, dispatches store actions, orchestrates side effects; minimal markup.
- **Presentational** (`features/<feature>/components/` or `shared/components/`): pure UI, only `@Input() / @Output()` or `input() / output()`, no HTTP, no store dispatch.

### Folder Layout (feature-based, one folder per component)
```
features/<feature>/
├── pages/         # Routed smart components
├── components/    # Smart + dumb components
├── services/      # @Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
├── store/         # NgRx state/actions/reducer/selectors/effects/component-store
├── models/        # Interfaces, DTOs, types
├── guards/        # CanActivateFn / CanMatchFn
└── interceptors/  # Functional HTTP interceptors
shared/            # Cross-cutting components, directives, pipes, tokens, utils
core/              # App config, singleton services, app-level guards/interceptors
component-name/
├── component-name.component.ts
├── component-name.component.html      # inline only if < 10 lines
├── component-name.component.scss
├── component-name.component.spec.ts
└── index.ts                           # barrel export
```

### Component Conventions
- Selector: kebab-case with feature prefix (e.g. `iid-vehicle-list`)
- `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on every component
- Prefer signal-based `input()` / `output()` / `model()` for new code
- New control-flow only: `@if`, `@for` (always with `track`), `@switch`, `@defer` — never `*ngIf`/`*ngFor`
- DI: prefer `inject()` over constructor injection; use `InjectionToken<T>` for non-class deps

---

## Styling
- External `*.component.scss` only — **no inline** `style="..."` or `[style]` bindings
- **No `::ngDeep`** — use CSS custom properties for theming overrides
- Global resets/typography/theme in `src/styles.scss` only
- Responsive: SCSS flexbox/grid + media queries or CDK `BreakpointObserver`

---

## TypeScript & Quality
- `strict: true` + `strictTemplates: true`; no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- `readonly` on immutable props, `as const` for literals
- RxJS: functional operators (`switchMap`, `combineLatest`); avoid raw `.subscribe()` without cleanup
- Handle `loading` / `error` / `empty` states in every template
- Generic UI in `shared/components/` wrapped over Material primitives
- SRP — components < 150 lines, extract subcomponents when growing

---

## Do
Co-locate `.ts/.html/.scss/.spec.ts` + barrel · separate container vs presentational · NgRx Component Store for server state, Signals for local · new control-flow syntax · `OnPush` + `track` · `takeUntilDestroyed()` or `async`/`toSignal()`.

## Don't
Inline styles · NgModules for new code · legacy `*ngIf`/`*ngFor` · `any` / `@ts-ignore` · server caching in component signals · HTTP inside presentational components · unhandled `.subscribe()` · `::ngDeep`.
